# OpenWrt MCP + SSH

## Prefer MCP

When namespace **`user-openwrt`** is available:

1. `GetDynamicTools` → read schema → `CallDynamicTool`
2. Start with **`openwrt_test_connection`**
3. Use MCP for UCI, apk, firewall, ping, DNS, logs, interfaces

Setup: `openwrt-packages/scripts/setup-openwrt-mcp.sh` — skill **`openwrt-mcp-ssh`**.

## UCI safety

- Stage with `openwrt_uci_set`; never assume live until `openwrt_uci_commit`
- Commit **one package** at a time; use **safety rollback** for `network`, `wireless`, `firewall`
- **`openwrt_uci_confirm`** only after user-visible verification
- Ask before **`openwrt_reboot`**

## APK not opkg

ImmortalWrt 25.x uses **`apk`**. Custom feed packages may require GitHub Pages feed, not snapshots CDN.

## SSH when MCP has no tool

| Need | SSH |
|------|-----|
| mcudd binary deploy | `ssh … 'cat > /tmp/mcudd.new'` (no `scp` / sftp) |
| RDCP link test | `/usr/lib/mcud/mcud-link-test.sh` |
| Local files `/tmp/mcud_*` | `cat` on router |
| Blocky raw API | `wget -qO- http://127.0.0.1:4000/...` |
| I2C / sysfs | `i2cdetect`, `/sys/...` |

Default: `ssh root@192.168.8.1` with project SSH key.

## Do not

- Run firmware builds on macOS host (use `build_immortalwrt` Docker)
- Destructive overlay/git operations without explicit user request
- Flash ESP32 over USB while mcudd holds the same UART (stop mcudd, flash, unplug USB-C, start mcudd)
- Change swipe → LuCI `/tmp/mcud_active_screen` logic (frozen; skill `mcu-display-cm5`)
